# Packages Decorator Documentation Requirements

- Every time a decorator is created or introduced in package code, include a documentation block.
- Document decorator functionality in terms of purpose and runtime behavior, not just syntax.
- At minimum, document:
  - what the decorator does
  - required arguments/metadata and accepted values
  - side effects (for example, metadata registration, validation hooks, behavioral overrides)
  - when it executes and how it affects the decorated class/method/property/parameter
  - usage example for maintainers

## Required Template

Use or adapt this block above new decorator declarations/usages:

```ts
/**
 * Purpose: <what this decorator enforces or enables>
 * Target: <class | method | property | parameter>
 * Arguments: <name/type/defaults/allowed values>
 * Runtime behavior: <when it runs and what it changes>
 * Side effects: <metadata, validation, injection, or other impacts>
 * Example: <short usage snippet>
 */
```
